@startuml
' ============================================================
' 📄 File: runtime_error_component.puml
' 🧱 Layer: Infrastructure (Runtime)
' 🎯 Purpose: Represent P1_Error runtime system and its relations
' 🧑 Author: Mohamed Ali
' 🗓️ Created: 2025-10-21
' ============================================================

!define USE_CUSTOM_THEME
!include ../../config/style.puml

FA6_BUG(ERROR, "P1_Error", component, #E2C22F)
FA6_CUBE(DOMERR, "P1_DomainError", component, #D97A2B)
FA6_GEAR(LOGGER, "P1_Logger", component, #E5C55F)
FA6_BELL(NOTIFIER, "P1_Notifier", component, #C2C2C2)
FA6_DATABASE(FACTORY, "P1_S2_TaskRepositoryFactory", component, #4DA6FF)

' ----------------------
' Relationships
' ----------------------
ERROR --> DOMERR : converts to/from
LOGGER --> ERROR : logs runtime failures
NOTIFIER --> ERROR : displays user feedback
FACTORY --> ERROR : raises runtime errors
FACTORY --> LOGGER : logs initialization results
FACTORY --> NOTIFIER : shows fallback messages

' ----------------------
' Notes and Tags
' ----------------------
note right of ERROR
  🧩 Represents runtime/infrastructure error model
  Contains:
  - code (enum)
  - message
  - context (optional map)
  - conversion helpers
end note

note bottom of FACTORY
  ⚙️ Factory uses P1_Error to:
  - detect DB init/auth issues
  - trigger fallback (InMemory)
  - log + notify failures
end note

@enduml
